  formulation names the finite labels and states the per-label constants
  directly. These are reorganized arguments rather than literal source
  theorem statements.

  <section|Correspondence and construction
  chain><label|correspondence-and-construction-chain>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Article
  result or step>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified
  declaration>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned path>>|<cell|<strong|Classification>>>|<row|<cell|Installed
  kernel and exact install-difference identity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.install>;
  <verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.install_step>; <verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.cross_atlas>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Crossing.lean>>|<cell|Proved
  source input; article rederives the coefficient change and residue
  decomposition explicitly>>|<row|<cell|Per-label row/column/difference atlas
  interpretation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.RowCost>;
  <verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.ColCost>; <verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.Atlas>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Atlas.lean>>|<cell|Definition
  inspected>>|<row|<cell|Composition and finite-label cost
  factors>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.row_sandwich>;
  <verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.col_sandwich>; <verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.all_sandwich>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Coin.lean>;
  bind estimates in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Tails.lean>>|<cell|Proved
  source input; article supplies an ordinary weighted convolution
  proof>>|<row|<cell|Complete response atlas from <verbatim|Deep> and covered
  beds>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.predictor_atlas>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Coin.lean>>|<cell|Proved
  in source; exact inputs are <verbatim|V.Deep \<alpha\> C z>,
  <verbatim|H.covered \<alpha\> C>, <verbatim|H'.covered \<theta\> X>,
  <verbatim|1\<leq\>z>, odd <verbatim|L>, width comparisons and nonnegative
  costs. It consumes <verbatim|V.T> base strip at
  <verbatim|C/L\<twosuperior\>> and four first-difference strips at
  <verbatim|C/L\<threesuperior\>>; no higher <verbatim|Deep> fields are used
  for this estimate. Its output cost is <verbatim|pre Faces Faces C
  (exp(4\<sigma\>)*C) X>, i.e. <verbatim|\|Faces\|\<twosuperior\>
  exp(4\<sigma\>) C\<twosuperior\> X> for equal face
  types.>>|<row|<cell|Publicly priced response
  atlas>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pert.Bulk.priced_atlas>; caller in
  <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.to_here>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Coin.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG08/Flat/World.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|priced_atlas> only
  projects <verbatim|Horizon.Suffices.costs> and <verbatim|.rows> into
  <verbatim|predictor_atlas>; the latter performs the quantitative
  estimate.>>|<row|<cell|Tower receipt specification>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.Towers.Deep>;
  <verbatim|YM.Craft.Donate>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/PREC/Stacks.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Craft.lean>>|<cell|Definition inspected.
  <verbatim|Deep> asks for <verbatim|mn,o,mf> strips and every
  <verbatim|A0,T> advance up to a finite order; <verbatim|Donate> is the
  preserved <verbatim|A0,T> part.>>|<row|<cell|Bed construction from a
  flight>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Flight.duo>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Primal.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|duo.T>
  is the actual cross-stencil <verbatim|meshBook (wire k) 2 [] P>; it is not
  <verbatim|rollFunds>.>>|<row|<cell|Entrywise momentum-space estimate for
  the tower wire>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Flight.wire_budget>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Cable.lean>>|<cell|Quantitative
  producer proved in source. For each finite family of flights <verbatim|F :
  \<iota\> \<rightarrow\> Flight j t> and selected aliases <verbatim|l i :
  Site (F i).L>, positive coupling <verbatim|k>, and <verbatim|j,t\<geq\>4>,
  it proves <verbatim|Pay (fun i =\<gtr\> decay j (l i)) (fun i p =\<gtr\>
  wire k (F i) p (l i))>. <verbatim|Pay.tap> bounds each complex matrix entry
  by a Moderate function, uniformly over the family and momentum. The proof
  splits on zero/nonzero aliases using <verbatim|copper_budget> and
  <verbatim|stake_budget>, whose factors are assembled by
  sum/product/quotient bounds for flux, heart, tail, masks, and train
  denominators.>>|<row|<cell|Uniform thread receipt for all
  flights>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.secure_both>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Secured>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Strands.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|secure_both>
  applies <verbatim|wire_budget> to the sigma-finite index of every flight
  and alias, then records reciprocal-shift and reflection identities. These
  are formal hypotheses of the <verbatim|Secured> record, each proved by
  <verbatim|knots_shift> and <verbatim|knots_reflect>.>>|<row|<cell|Laurent
  strip receipts for every actual difference
  word>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Secured.bankCost>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Secured.traverse>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.Free.Secured.honored>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Sprout.lean>>|<cell|Proved
  source input. <verbatim|bankCost> applies <verbatim|matrix_cover> to
  entrywise <verbatim|Pay>, obtaining <verbatim|C/(L)^{e+\|u\|}> uniformly
  over flights. <verbatim|traverse> identifies true cover differences with
  the mesh-book advance including carry. <verbatim|honored> intersects the
  finitely many widths/costs for all words of length at most
  <verbatim|j\<minus\>2> by <verbatim|staple>. For <verbatim|e=2>, this gives
  exactly <verbatim|Donate> for <verbatim|duo.T> including empty and
  one-letter words.>>|<row|<cell|Catalog containing these
  receipts>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.pledges> and fields
  <verbatim|Catalog.hop>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Priced.lean>>|<cell|Proved
  in source. The hop uses <verbatim|secure_both> plus
  <verbatim|Secured.honored> for the tower strips; <verbatim|Flight.frontier>
  supplies a different strip/positivity bound for <verbatim|rollFunds>. The
  two are not interchangeable.>>|<row|<cell|Rack carrying the receipts to the
  horizon>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Free.shelves>;
  <verbatim|YM.Bid.Craft.Rack.legs>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Rack.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Craft.lean>>|<cell|Proved transport:
  <verbatim|shelves> uses <verbatim|Catalog.hop> to fill
  <verbatim|Rack.legs>.>>|<row|<cell|Full horizon <verbatim|Deep>
  records>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Bid.pinning>; downstream
  <verbatim|retarget_arc>; <verbatim|Horizon.Suffices.costs>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Craft.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/UVExtension/Case/Valence.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/PREC/Stacks.lean>>|<cell|Proved transport/construction:
  <verbatim|pinning> calls <verbatim|Work.F08.answer>; that theorem generates
  the new <verbatim|mf,mn,o> estimates and passes the old <verbatim|T,A0>
  <verbatim|Deep> receipts through. <verbatim|retarget_arc> then transports
  them using width/cost monotonicity.>>|<row|<cell|Public construction
  selection and consumption of a suffices
  horizon>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>;
  <verbatim|YM.Integration.ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.on_run>>|<cell|<verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|constructionRun>
  selects a run with <verbatim|R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>;
  <verbatim|on_run> uses the already selected <verbatim|R.alloy.B.plan> on
  the actual horizon. This audit does not replay that larger selection
  theorem. The <verbatim|FundedPredictionSupply.Always> argument is
  definitionally <verbatim|True> and is not the source of the tower strip
  estimates.>>>>>

  <section|Mathematical proof notes><label|mathematical-proof-notes>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>For a fixed input point, the row sum is reindexed by
    <math|z=y-\<rho\><rsub|L><around|(|x|)>>. The centered lift has one
    coordinate of magnitude at most <math|<around|(|L-1|)>/2>, so
    <math|<around|\||\<ell\><rsub|L><around|(|r|)>|\|><rsub|1>/L\<leqslant\>2>;
    the difference from the source's <math|+4> margin is harmless. The same
    substitution on a fixed output column first decomposes each input
    uniquely as <math|x=\<ell\><rsub|L><around|(|r|)>+L*v>; summing over
    <math|v> costs the original strip bound, then summing over residues
    contributes exactly <math|L<rsup|4>>. The one-step difference is exactly
    installation of <verbatim|forwardC>, requiring the odd centered-lift
    carry identity.

    <item>The sandwich proof uses <math|d<rsub|L><around|(|x,y|)>\<leqslant\>d<rsub|L><around|(|x+u,y+v|)>+<around|\||u|\|><rsub|1>/L+<around|\||v|\|><rsub|1>>,
    absorbs each displacement in its stencil strip using both
    <math|\<sigma\>/L\<leqslant\>\<alpha\>> and
    <math|\<sigma\>\<leqslant\>\<alpha\>>, and sums over the two intermediate
    face-label sets. The input difference is obtained by subtracting the two
    convolution formulas with the same summation variables; the difference
    acts on the installed tower kernel at the shifted inner input point, with
    no reindexing of the first displacement.

    <item>The publication proof is therefore not blocked at
    <verbatim|Rack.legs>: the local tower cross-kernel receipt is actually
    generated from the wire entrywise <verbatim|Pay> estimate. The high-level
    public selection uses that proved route via the stored horizon plan,
    although this audit does not audit every other component of the selection
    theorem.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Literature search><label|literature-search>

  Searched <verbatim|blueprint/background> for <verbatim|Wilson>,
  <verbatim|atlas>, <verbatim|Schur>, <verbatim|kernel>, <verbatim|strip>,
  <verbatim|Laurent>, and <verbatim|RG>. The only matching background note
  was <verbatim|blueprint/background/su2-simplicity.md>, unrelated to the
  weighted lattice kernel estimates. No outside theorem is required for the
  arguments in this unit; the period decomposition and weighted convolution
  bounds are proved directly. The inspected Lean estimates give a fully
  formal source proof, but the ordinary-mathematics exposition remains a
  draft awaiting independent review.

  <section|Commands and limits><label|commands-and-limits>

  Read-only source inspection commands run in the isolated clone included:

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|rg -n "predictor_atlas\|all_sandwich\|cross_atlas\|def
    install\|def Atlas\|def RowCost\|def ColCost"
    Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Atlas.lean Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Crossing.lean
    Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Coin.lean> \V located the atlas, installation, and
    predictor declarations.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,250p' Lean/YM/Pert/Bulk/Coin.lean> \V read the
    strip-composition bounds and exact predictor hypotheses/cost.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,175p' Lean/YM/PREC/Stacks.lean> \V checked
    <verbatim|Bed>, <verbatim|Towers>, <verbatim|forwardC>, <verbatim|Deep>,
    and <verbatim|Horizon.Suffices> meanings.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,200p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Sprout.lean>
    and <verbatim|sed -n '1,140p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/MatrixPay.lean>
    \V checked the strip extraction chain from weighted entries.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,155p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Cable.lean>,
    <verbatim|sed -n '1,175p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Strands.lean>,
    <verbatim|sed -n '1,120p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Priced.lean>, and
    <verbatim|sed -n '1,160p' Lean/YM/Next/FREE_KERNELS/Rack.lean> \V
    inspected the concrete <verbatim|wire_budget> supplier and its public
    transport.

    <item><verbatim|sed -n '1,220p' Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>
    and <verbatim|sed -n '1,115p' Lean/YM/Integration/ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.lean>
    \V checked the selected-run output and use of the actual stored plan.

    <item><verbatim|rg -n "Wilson\|atlas\|Schur\|kernel\|strip\|Laurent\|RG"
    blueprint/background> \V focused literature-note search.
  </itemize-minus>

  No Lean build, manuscript build, blueprint checker, or external-source
  search was run for this unit. The imported Lean source revision recorded in
  <verbatim|source/upstream.json> is <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  The reviewed declarations and paths must be rechecked against that imported
  source before acceptance.

